---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = baseUrl.endsWith('/') ? baseUrl : `${baseUrl}/`;
---

<Layout
  title="Contact me | Gerardo Ramirez"
  description="How to reach Gerardo Ramirez for consulting, advisory work, speaking, and collaboration."
  canonical={`${base}contact`}
>
  <Navigation />

  <main class="page-content" aria-label="Content">
    <article class="wrapper post">
      <header class="post-header">
        <h1 class="post-title">Contact me</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="post-content">
        <p>
          Communication is easier when expectations are clear. This page is a short reference
          for the best ways to reach me — not a rigid set of rules.
        </p>

        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          The best way to reach me is via email.
          I try to respond thoughtfully, especially for consulting, advisory work,
          speaking invitations, and collaboration ideas.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your note is long or non-urgent, I may take a few days.
          If I haven’t replied in a week, feel free to follow up.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:hello@gerardoramirez.info">hello@gerardoramirez.info</a>
        </p>

        <h2>What I’m open to</h2>
        <p>I’m especially interested in conversations about:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Enterprise integrations and partner engineering</li>
          <li>Architecture reviews and technical strategy</li>
          <li>Applied AI systems going from prototype to production</li>
          <li>Early-stage product building and developer experience</li>
          <li>Speaking and workshops on AI engineering, architecture, and leadership</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Social media</h2>
        <p>
          I use social media lightly. You’re welcome to follow along, but email is still
          the most reliable way to reach me.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>LinkedIn:</strong>
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gerardo-ramirez-09/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gerardo-ramirez-09</a>
            — useful for professional context; I prefer email for real conversations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>GitHub:</strong>
            <a href="https://github.com/gerardoramirez" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gerardoramirez</a>
            — best place to see what I’m building in public.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Twitter / X:</strong> I check it occasionally; please don’t rely on DMs.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>tl;dr:</em> follow me where you like, but reach me via email.</p>

        <h2>Scheduling</h2>
        <p>
          For scheduled calls or meetings, please send a calendar invite once we’ve agreed on a time.
          A short agenda in the invite helps a lot.
        </p>

        <h2>A note</h2>
        <p>
          I’m systematic, but not inflexible. Some of the best collaborations start as informal,
          open-ended conversations. If something interesting is on your mind, write.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content {
    padding: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-xl);
  }

  .post {
    animation: fade-rise 0.7s ease both;
  }

  .post-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .post-title {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .post-content {
    animation: fade-rise 0.75s ease 0.08s both;
  }

  .post-content :global(h2) {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
  }

  .post-content :global(p),
  .post-content :global(ul) {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    max-width: 40em;
  }

  .post-content :global(ul) {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content :global(li) {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }

  .post-content :global(strong) {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .post-content :global(h2) {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
